SUMMARY:[Ceremonies & Commemorations] Remembrance Day: West Kelowna (Legion
  Branch #288)
DESCRIPTION:Category: Ceremonies & Commemorations\n\nHonour parade at 10 a.
 m.\, service 10:45 a.m.–noon\, moment of silence at 11. Hosted by Royal 
 Canadian Legion Westbank Branch #288. The MP and local councils usually at
 tend. Times are based on past years\; confirm closer to the date.\n\nSourc
 e / more info: https://www.tourismkelowna.com/events/annual-events-festiva
 ls/fall/indigenous-veterans-day-remembrance-day/
LOCATION:Royal LePage Place\, 2760 Cameron Rd\, West Kelowna\, BC
CATEGORIES:Ceremonies & Commemorations
URL:https://www.tourismkelowna.com/events/annual-events-festivals/fall/indi
 genous-veterans-day-remembrance-day/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
